 Automatic Undo Management (AUM)

Oracle uses Automatic Undo Management by default.

SHOW PARAMETER undo_management;

Oracle automatically manages:

Undo Segments
Undo Space
Undo Reuse
-----------------------------------------------------------
Undo Tablespace

Undo information is stored inside the Undo Tablespace.

Check:

SHOW PARAMETER undo_tablespace;

Example:

UNDOTBS1

Undo is required for:

Flashback Query
Flashback Table
Flashback Version Query
Flashback Transaction Query
Read Consistency
Transaction Rollback
-----------------------------------------------------------
UNDO_RETENTION

SHOW PARAMETER undo_retention;

900

Oracle attempts to retain undo information for 900 seconds (15 minutes).
-----------------------------------------------------------
RETENTION NOGUARANTEE (Default)

By default, Oracle may overwrite old undo data before the retention period expires if the Undo Tablespace becomes full.

Therefore, UNDO_RETENTION is only a target, not a guarantee.
-----------------------------------------------------------
RETENTION GUARANTEE

ALTER TABLESPACE undotbs1
RETENTION GUARANTEE;

Oracle guarantees that undo data will be preserved for the specified retention period.

If the Undo Tablespace becomes full, new DML operations may fail instead of overwriting existing undo.
-----------------------------------------------------------
Undo Advisor

Oracle Enterprise Manager (OEM) provides Undo Advisor.
in TOAD : Database -> Diagnose -> Undo Advisor(OEM)
in oracle SQL Server -> automatic undo managment

It helps DBAs:
Estimate the required Undo Tablespace size.
Recommend an appropriate UNDO_RETENTION value.
Analyze undo usage.
-----------------------------------------------------------
Recycle Bin
When a table is dropped:

DROP TABLE employees;
Oracle moves the table to the Recycle Bin instead of permanently deleting it.

Recover the table:
FLASHBACK TABLE employees TO BEFORE DROP;
-----------------------------------------------------------
Archive Logs store Redo information (database changes).

They are used for:
RMAN Recovery
Media Recovery
Complete Recovery

Archive Logs do not store a complete image of the database.

BUT 

Flashback Logs store before-images of modified data blocks.
They are created only when Flashback Database is enabled.

Flashback Logs are stored in the: Fast Recovery Area (FRA)
They are used only by Flashback Database



| Archive Log                  | Flashback Log                                     |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| Stores redo (changes made)   | Stores before-images of data blocks               |
| Used by RMAN Recovery        | Used by Flashback Database                        |
| Required for media recovery  | Required for rewinding the database               |
| Generated in ARCHIVELOG mode | Generated only when Flashback Database is enabled |

-----------------------------------------------------------
Flashback Retention

SHOW PARAMETER db_flashback_retention_target;
1440

Meaning:
Oracle attempts to keep Flashback Logs for 1440 minutes (24 hours).
Like UNDO_RETENTION, this is a target, not a guaranteed value.
Actual retention depends on available FRA space.



